```java
public boolean isPowerOfThree(int n) {
    // Negative numbers are not powers of 3, as the base must be positive.
    if (n <= 0) {
        return false;
    }

    // The largest power of 3 that can be represented by an unsigned 32-bit integer is 2^32 / 3 = 1162261467.
    // Therefore, we can divide n by the largest power of 3 to find if it is a power of 3.
    while (n % 3 == 0) {
        n /= 3;
    }

    return n == 1;
}
```

This solution works by checking if the integer `n` is a non-zero positive number, and then successively dividing `n` by 3 until it is no longer divisible by 3 (i.e., `n % 3 != 0`). If the result of this process is 1, then `n` is a power of three. This approach avoids using loops or recursion.

